source markdown %23%20A%20heading%0A%0AA%20paragraph%20under%20the%20heading%20with%20enough%20words%20in%20it%20to%20run%20to%20several%20lines%20when%20the%20measure%20is%20a%20column's,%20which%20is%20what%20gives%20the%20splitter%20legal%20places%20to%20cut.%0A%0A-%20One%20item.%0A-%20A%20second%20item.%0A-%20A%20third,%20and%20these%20three%20with%20the%20gaps%20between%20them%20are%20one%20unbreakable%20run.%0A%0A%23%23%20A%20second%20heading%0A%0AThe%20paragraph%20after%20it.%20A%20block%20boundary%20is%20a%20kern%20with%20no%20glue%20behind%20it,%20so%20no%20column%20ends%20between%20a%20heading%20and%20its%20first%20line,%20nor%20between%20two%20list%20items%20of%20one%20line%20each.%0A%0A```%0Acode%20line%20one%0Acode%20line%20two%0Acode%20line%20three%0A```%0A%0AA%20closing%20paragraph%20that%20is%20also%20long%20enough%20to%20be%20divided%20between%20two%20columns%20if%20the%20cut%20happens%20to%20fall%20inside%20it.%0A
